# Q3: Train Round Trips

**Step 1: Find the time for one one-way trip.**

$$\text{Time} = \frac{\text{Distance}}{\text{Speed}} = \frac{200 \text{ km}}{60 \text{ km/h}} = \frac{10}{3} \text{ hours} \approx 3.33 \text{ hours}$$

**Step 2: Find the time for one round trip.**

A round trip = 2 × 200 km = 400 km

$$\text{Time} = \frac{400 \text{ km}}{60 \text{ km/h}} = \frac{20}{3} \text{ hours} \approx 6.67 \text{ hours}$$

**Step 3: Find how many round trips fit in 24 hours.**

$$\frac{24 \text{ hours}}{\frac{20}{3} \text{ hours per round trip}} = 24 \times \frac{3}{20} = \frac{72}{20} = 3.6$$

**Step 4: Round down** (since the train can't complete a partial trip).

**Answer: The train can make 3 complete round trips in a full day.**

*(Note: After 3 round trips, 20 hours are used, leaving 4 hours — enough for one more one-way trip, but not a complete round trip.)* [end of text]


